# Never Store Plain Passwords!

In the example, we used `{noop}` to indicate no password encoding (only for learning). In production, use a password encoder like `BCryptPasswordEncoder`.

```java
@Bean
public PasswordEncoder passwordEncoder() {
    return new BCryptPasswordEncoder();
}
```

Then create users with encoded passwords:

```java
User.withUsername("user")
    .password(passwordEncoder().encode("password"))
    .roles("USER")
    .build();
```
